# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# Without this file the context is ~1.2 GB: `.tools/go` is a vendored Go
# toolchain (252 MB) and `.cache/` holds the module + build caches (896 MB).
# Both are local development conveniences that the multi-stage build has no
# use for — the build stage starts from golang:1.25-alpine and runs its own
# `go mod download`. Shipping them just made every `docker build` upload a
# gigabyte before doing any work.

# Local Go toolchain and caches (see GO_ENVIRONMENT_zh.md).
.tools/
.cache/

# Build artifacts — the image builds its own.
bin/

# VCS and CI.
.git/
.github/
.gitignore

# Docs and examples that do not belong in an image layer.
# NOTE: examples/data/ is deliberately NOT excluded — config.example.yaml
# references it, so `docker run` with the sample config works out of the box.
*.md
docs/
deploy/

# Local operator config: real deployments bind-mount their own.
config.yaml
tile-cache/
